From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SheepyLord <37598021+SheepyLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 15:30:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Bound the DDS readers and fix the review's other runtime
 findings

The pre-release review (R19) found that a DDS file in any loaded mod could
corrupt the game's memory, and a few smaller runtime faults.

- H1: the partial DDS loader took the mip count unchecked and wrote one size
  per level into a table of 16 (17 or more overwrote the rest of the object:
  the data size, the file handle, then the vtable), and GLI's fallback copied
  as many bytes as the header claimed from a buffer as large as the file.
  Both now check the headers with gli::detail::dds_check_layout before they
  read the data: a format GLI knows, sides of 1 to 65536, at most 16 levels
  and no more than the sides allow (a count of 0 reads as 1, as Microsoft's
  loaders read it), at most 2048 layers, 1 to 6 cube faces, and data sizes
  summed in 64 bits with overflow checks that fit in the file. A volume's
  levels count their depth. The partial loader's file size is 64-bit, every
  read is checked, a subresource the file lacks is placed nowhere, and the
  mapped file must still hold the checked data. GLI's reader refuses empty,
  short and unmeasurable files; the fallback reads DDS only (gli::load also
  tried KMG and KTX, which copy unchecked). DdsFileParser moved to
  rtx_dds_file_parser.h for the new test_dds_reader (crafted headers: 17, 18
  and 2^31 mips, short files, huge array sizes).
- F-01: RtxOption::getCopy() copies a value under the update mutex. The
  menus' string reads on the game's thread use it (RemixGui::InputText, the
  texture menu's legacy-emissive and thin-wall strings, the capture stage
  name, the menu language), and so do the fallback-mod list and the capture
  name with its timestamp. The capture name box copies at most its buffer.
  Stress test in test_rtx_option_threads.
- F-03: a texture the asset cache shares takes the strongest preload its
  users ask for (PreloadStrength in rtx_texture_budget.h): a stronger
  request raises it from any thread, and the texture's next addTexture loads
  it as that preload, pinned and whole from that frame.
- F-04: the middle deck's patch mask is probed along the ray at most a
  quarter of a patch apart (3 to 16 probes; a ray that crosses the deck
  within half a patch keeps the three of before), the deck is skipped only
  when every probe is empty, and the cover is interpolated between them.
- F-05: the middle deck's moon-shadow taps read the patch mask where they
  are, not the shaded sample's.
- R-01: a config file saved through a link keeps its previous contents in a
  backup beside it until the in-place rewrite completes; a failed rewrite
  puts them back.
- R-02: rtx.gmod.eyeWhiteBrightness says it scales all scene-adaptive
  emission (ADR 0088's design). RtxOptions.md.
- R-03: the float option parser refuses NaN and infinities, and a float
  vector keeps its old value whole when a component is refused.
